# Story: As a terminal planner, I want each container to have at most one open booking, so that two trucks are never sent for the same container. If a container already has a booking that is BOOKED, another booking for it (by anyone, for any slot) is refused with DUPLICATE_ACTIVE_BOOKING. After the first booking is cancelled the container can be booked again.

@draft
Feature: Preventing Duplicate Bookings

  Scenario Outline: Booking a container with an existing active booking is refused
    Given I am a driver
    And another driver has already booked that slot
    When I book that slot for container "<container>"
    Then the outcome is "DUPLICATE_ACTIVE_BOOKING"

    Examples:
      | container |
      | CONT123  |
      | CONT456  |

  Scenario Outline: Booking a container after cancelling an existing booking succeeds
    Given I am a driver
    And I have booked that slot for a valid container "<container>"
    When I cancel my booking
    Then the outcome is "CANCELLED"
    And another driver books a different slot for the same container "<container>"
    Then their booking is refused because "DUPLICATE_ACTIVE_BOOKING"
    When I book that slot for container "<container>"
    Then the outcome is "CONFIRMED"

    Examples:
      | container |
      | CONT123  |
      | CONT456  |
